\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Evaluation metrics. Confusion-matrix quantities reflect snow as the positive class. True positive (TP) and true negative (TN) are correctly called snow and rain, false positive (FP) is rain called snow, false negative (FN) is snow called rain, and $N$ is the number of rain and snow observations. Probability metrics use the calibrated $p(\mathrm  {snow})$, written $p_i$ for observation $i$ with outcome $y_i \in \{0,1\}$ (1 = snow). Envelope metrics use the uncertainty band of Equation~\ref {eq:band} and are the only ones computed over all $N_{\mathrm  {all}}$ observations, mix included, where $M$ is the number of observer-reported mixed events, $M_{\mathrm  {in}}$ those inside the band, and $F$ all predictions inside it. Every metric is also computed on the near-freezing subset ($|T_w| \le \ensuremath  {2\,^{\circ }\mathrm  {C}}$).}}{8}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:metrics}{{2}{8}{}{table.2}{}}
