\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Ablation study: held-out test performance by feature configuration, with 95\% cluster-bootstrap confidence intervals. The predictors retained by each configuration are listed in the third column, using $T_a$, $T_d$ and $T_w$ for air, dewpoint and wet-bulb temperature, E for elevation, P for the IMERG probability of liquid precipitation, and M for the three leakage-safe MRoS phase surfaces, which count as three predictors; $n$ is the resulting predictor count. All configurations share kriged predictors, beta calibration, and identical splits, so differences are attributable to the feature set alone. Decimal metrics omit the leading zero and NF denotes the near-freezing subset ($|T_w| \le \ensuremath  {2\,^{\circ }\mathrm  {C}}$). Note that these absolute intervals overlap between configurations even where the paired difference is clear of zero, so Figure~\ref {fig:ablation-ci}, not this table, is the basis for every significance claim in the text.}}{11}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:ablation}{{4}{11}{}{table.4}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {d}Benchmarking}{11}{}\protected@file@percent }
